  "id": "guttman-scale",
  "term": "Guttman scale",
  "definition": "A Guttman scale is a way of arranging items in a single order of difficulty or endorsement so that endorsing or answering a later item implies that all earlier, easier, or prerequisite items would also be endorsed or answered. In such a scale, people with the same total score are expected to show the same response pattern.",
